{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ונקדשתי בתוך בני ישראל", :translit "v'nikdashti b'toch b'nei yisra'el", :gloss "and I shall be sanctified in the midst of the children of Israel"} {:he "זהו אין אומרים קדושה פחות מעשרה", :translit "zehu ein omrim kedushah pachot mi'asarah", :gloss "this is: one does not recite Kedushah with fewer than ten"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "ונקדשתי בתוך בני ישראל", :b "זהו אין אומרים קדושה פחות מעשרה"}], :frame {:text "The recitation of Kedushah requires a minyan of ten adult men, as stated in Berakhot 21b deriving from the word 'among' (תוך) in Leviticus 22:32. The verse 'I shall be sanctified among the children of Israel' is read by the Sifrei (Bemidbar 143) as a command for public sanctification, and Berakhot 21b takes the word 'among' (תוך/בתוך) to imply a congregation of ten, based on the use of the same word in Numbers 16:21 regarding Korah's assembly.", :sources ["Berakhot 21b" "Sifrei Bemidbar 143" "Leviticus 22:32" "Numbers 16:21"]}} {:quotes [{:he "בתוך בני ישראל", :translit "b'toch b'nei yisra'el", :gloss "in the midst of the children of Israel"} {:he "שברוב עם הדרת מלך", :translit "sheb'rov am hadrat melech", :gloss "for in the multitude of people is the king's splendor"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Adjacent parashah (Emor, Leviticus 23) lists the festivals, when people gather en masse — the verse's emphasis on 'among' foreshadows this."}], :frame {:text "Proverbs 14:28 states 'ברוב עם הדרת מלך,' 'in the multitude of people is the king's splendor.' The Mishnah in Hagigah 3a describes how all Israel would assemble at the Temple on the pilgrimage festivals.", :sources ["Proverbs 14:28" "Hagigah 3a"]}} {:quotes [{:he "מקדשכם", :translit "mikdashchem", :gloss "your sanctuary"} {:he "שחייב אדם לטהר את עצמו ברגל", :translit "shechayav adam l'taher et atzmo b'regel", :gloss "that a person is obligated to purify himself on the festival"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Adjacent verse moves from 'My sanctuary' (22:32) to 'appointed times of YHWH' (23:2), hinting at the festival purity obligation."}], :frame {:text "The Mishnah in Hagigah 3a–3b records that all Israel are obligated in the mitzvah of appearance at the Temple on pilgrimage festivals, and Chagigah 3a teaches that everyone must purify themselves beforehand for the festival.", :sources ["Hagigah 3a" "Hagigah 3b"]}}], :arithmetic [{:a-value 1901, :b-value 1900, :lens :standard, :equal? false, :kind :gematria, :b "זהו אין אומרים קדושה פחות מעשרה", :by :selah, :colel? true, :a "ונקדשתי בתוך בני ישראל"} {:kind :other, :note "Adjacent parashah (Emor, Leviticus 23) lists the festivals, when people gather en masse — the verse's emphasis on 'among' foreshadows this.", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Adjacent verse moves from 'My sanctuary' (22:32) to 'appointed times of YHWH' (23:2), hinting at the festival purity obligation.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:25:09.635600766Z", :model "glm-5.2"}